{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Reduce fuel duty for HGV owner drivers & small hauliers",
        "additional_details": "Owner drivers keep Britain moving \u2014 delivering food, supplies and essentials every day. Fuel makes up 40\u201350% of owner-drivers\u2019 costs. While big fleets can get discounts, owner-drivers cannot \u2014 and pay more per litre and earn less per mile than big fleet owners. We believe the 5p duty cut is not enough. Many drivers often work below minimum wage just to stay on the road. If owner-drives have to stop working, supply chains will suffer and prices rise for everyone.",
        "background": "We call on the Government to reduce fuel duty for HGV owner drivers and small operators across the UK to help deliver fair fuel support. ",
